# Lab 02: Add Port Range to Firewall

## Objective

As `user1` with `sudo` privileges on `server30`, permanently allow UDP ports `8000` through `8005` in the `trusted` firewalld zone. Verify the configuration using both the zone's XML file and `firewall-cmd`.

## Steps

Add the UDP port range to the permanent configuration of the `trusted` zone:

sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=trusted --add-port=8000-8005/udp

Reload firewalld to activate the permanent configuration:

sudo firewall-cmd --reload

Verify that the UDP port range is active:

sudo firewall-cmd --zone=trusted --list-ports

The output should include:

8000-8005/udp

The persistent zone configuration can also be viewed directly:

sudo cat /etc/firewalld/zones/trusted.xml

The XML file should contain an entry similar to:

<port protocol="udp" port="8000-8005"/>

## Result

UDP ports `8000` through `8005` were permanently allowed in the `trusted` zone. The configuration was activated with `firewall-cmd --reload` and verified through both `firewall-cmd` and the persistent zone XML file.
